{"availability":"available","full":"giovi321/ios-backup-machine","name":"ios-backup-machine","description":"Offline, portable and automatic iPhone backup system","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":509,"forks":27,"created":"2025-10-16T20:47:57Z","updated":"2026-10-07T13:20:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://giovi321.github.io/ios-backup-machine/","topics":[],"demo":"https://giovi321.github.io/ios-backup-machine/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:45.092Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:45.092Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:45.092Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:45.092Z","stars":509,"forks":27}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Plug in an iPhone and it backs up on its own. No iCloud, no iTunes, no computer, no account.","The whole appliance runs on a Radxa Zero 3W (an upgraded Raspberry Pi Zero W) with a small e-ink screen and a battery UPS. When you connect a phone, it runs an encrypted idevicebackup2 backup to the microSD card, shows progress and any errors on the display, and keeps a log you can read later. An optional rsync-over-SSH job ships each backup to a remote server, over WireGuard if you want it off your LAN.","Every backup stays on storage you control, and it can be restored anytime with tools from libimobiledevice."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/giovi321/ios-backup-machine/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"135d6c0782bfa9f9e86b0376e74bfebc7cca49725a8ad9f5e489adb7d9122b82","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:45.316Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:45.316Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Plug in an iPhone and it backs up on its own. No iCloud, no iTunes, no computer, no account.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/giovi321/ios-backup-machine/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No iCloud, no iTunes, no computer, no account.",